    "readout_text": "To find \\( f(2023) \\), we first recognize that the function \\( f \\) is the Dirichlet inverse of the identity function \\( \\text{id} \\). This means that \\( f \\) satisfies the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{d \\mid n} d \\cdot f\\left(\\frac{n}{d}\\right) = 1\n\\]\n\nfor all positive integers \\( n \\). By analyzing the function for prime powers and using the multiplicative property of \\( f \\), we determine that for any prime \\( p \\) and integer \\( k \\geq 1 \\), \\( f(p^k) = 1 - p \\). Extending this to any integer \\( n \\) by factoring it into its prime components, we find that \\( f(n) \\) is the product of \\( (1 - p) \\) for each distinct prime \\( p \\) dividing \\( n \\).\n\nFactoring 2023, we find it is \\( 7 \\times 17^2 \\). The distinct prime factors are 7 and 17. Therefore,\n\n\\[\nf(2023) = (1 - 7)(1 - 17) = (-6)(-16) = 96\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{96}\n\\]",
